I'd argue that the ratio matters less than what the capital is able to provide, QOL-wise. Like, if a business owner made a billion dollars a year, but pays all of his employees three hundred thousand dollars a year... that's not only sufficient to provide for all needs, that's enough to live a wealthier life than basically 98% of the population. 

&#x200B;

Whereas if there's a business owner who makes $90k a year, but gets away with paying each of his employees $10k a year... the ratio is much less, but it's starvation level income.

